VortX backport: two merged upstream audio safety fixes without moving the custom base.

Base: 8c67647b50059406c5c0444903597281b81516cf.
Upstream:
  3b276cef9b74fa78d38ebe02a4fe7150cc252138
  https://github.com/mpv-player/mpv/commit/3b276cef9b74fa78d38ebe02a4fe7150cc252138
  ao_aaudio: fix the out-of-bounds read in the channel mask retry loop
  01a7420cbb4bfcb3ae275b864a8a734c61ee8831
  https://github.com/mpv-player/mpv/commit/01a7420cbb4bfcb3ae275b864a8a734c61ee8831
  ao_audiounit: keep the layout valid when a channel label is unknown

Both merged 2026-10-22; these are post-stable backports, not a new stable mpv release.
The hunks are verbatim upstream code. No DV/FEL, demux, HTTP, TLS, output-order,
sample-rate, passthrough, or avfoundation policy is changed. AAudio is Android-only;
AudioUnit is the iOS/tvOS fallback, not the Mac CoreAudio driver or preferred tvOS
avfoundation route. Source integration is not an activated shipping artifact.

--- a/audio/out/ao_aaudio.c
+++ b/audio/out/ao_aaudio.c
@@ -359,7 +359,7 @@ static int init(struct ao *ao)
             if (result != AAUDIO_ERROR_OUT_OF_RANGE) {
                 break;
             }
-        } while (i++ < MP_ARRAY_SIZE(aaudio_max_chnums));
+        } while (++i < MP_ARRAY_SIZE(aaudio_max_chnums));
 
         ao->channels = channels;
     } else {
--- a/audio/out/ao_audiounit.m
+++ b/audio/out/ao_audiounit.m
@@ -163,14 +163,16 @@ static bool init_audiounit(struct ao *ao)
         MP_VERBOSE(ao, "channel map: %i: %u\n", i, layout->mChannelDescriptions[i].mChannelLabel);
